# Storefront Cursor Rules

## File Organization

> **Note**: This section applies specifically to `vela/storefront/`

- **Always** organize components and templates following the existing pattern in `src/modules/`
- Structure: `src/modules/[module-name]/components/[component-name]/index.tsx`
- Structure: `src/modules/[module-name]/templates/[template-name]/index.tsx`
- Each component should have its own folder with an `index.tsx` file
- Use descriptive, kebab-case names for component folders

## Component Usage

> **Note**: This section applies specifically to `vela/storefront/`

- **Always** use components from `@medusajs/ui` package
- Import components directly: `import { Button, Heading, Text, Label, Container, Badge, clx, ... } from "@medusajs/ui"`
- Reference the Medusa UI documentation: https://docs.medusajs.com/ui
- Prefer Medusa UI components over custom implementations when available
- Use the `clx` utility from `@medusajs/ui` for conditional class names

## Styling and Classes

- **Always** use Tailwind CSS classes from `@medusajs/ui-preset`
- Use the `ui-` prefixed classes for consistent styling:
  - Backgrounds: `bg-ui-bg-base`, `bg-ui-bg-subtle`, `bg-ui-bg-field`, `bg-ui-bg-field-hover`
  - Text: `text-ui-fg-base`, `text-ui-fg-subtle`, `text-ui-fg-muted`
  - Borders: `border-ui-border-base`, `border-ui-border-interactive`
  - Focus states: `focus:shadow-borders-interactive-with-active`
- Avoid custom color values; use the design system tokens from the preset
- Follow the existing Tailwind configuration which extends `@medusajs/ui-preset`
- **Always** use Tailwind's default breakpoints for media queries: `sm`, `md`, `lg`, `xl`, `2xl` (e.g. `sm:flex`, `lg:hidden`). Do not use custom breakpoint names such as `small`, `xsmall`, `medium`, `large`, etc.

## Accessibility

- For buttons that only show an icon (no visible text), **always** add an `aria-label` that describes the action (e.g. `aria-label="Toggle sidebar"`, `aria-label="Open cart"`, `aria-label="Close menu"`).

## Code Patterns

- Use TypeScript for all components
- Export components as default exports
- Use React functional components with proper TypeScript typing
- Follow the existing patterns for props interfaces and component structure
- Use the `clx` utility for combining class names conditionally
- **Prefer `function` declarations or named function expressions** over anonymous arrow functions—for React components and for callbacks passed to hooks (`useEffect`, `useCallback`, `useMemo`, etc.). Named functions stack traces and refactors read better.
  - Example: `useEffect(function syncCart() { ... }, [deps])`, `useCallback(function handleSubmit() { ... }, [deps])`

## Medusa Admin Dashboard Customizations

> **Note**: This section applies specifically to `vela/backend/src/admin/`

- **Always** follow the same patterns as the existing Medusa UI in `medusa/packages/admin/dashboard/` when creating custom widgets or pages in `backend/src/admin/`
- For custom widgets (`backend/src/admin/widgets/`):
  - Export a React component as the default export
  - Export a `config` object using `defineWidgetConfig` from `@medusajs/admin-sdk` or `@medusajs/admin-shared`
  - Use `@medusajs/ui` components (Container, Heading, etc.) for consistent styling
  - Follow the widget injection zone patterns (e.g., `product.details.after`, `order.list.before`)
- For custom pages/routes (`backend/src/admin/routes/`):
  - Use layout components like `SingleColumnPage` from the dashboard package when appropriate
  - Use the `useExtension()` hook and `getWidgets()` method to integrate with the widget system
  - Follow the route structure patterns: `src/routes/[route-name]/[route-name].tsx` with an `index.ts` that exports the component
  - Use TypeScript for all route components
  - Reference existing routes in `medusa/packages/admin/dashboard/src/routes/` for structure and patterns

## Module Structure Examples

```
src/modules/
  [module-name]/
    components/
      [component-name]/
        index.tsx
    templates/
      [template-name].tsx
      or
      [template-name]/
        index.tsx
```

## Examples

### Good Component Structure

```tsx
import { Button, Heading, clx } from "@medusajs/ui";

type MyComponentProps = {
  title: string;
  className?: string;
};

function MyComponent({ title, className }: MyComponentProps) {
  return (
    <div className={clx("bg-ui-bg-subtle p-4", className)}>
      <Heading level="h1" className="text-ui-fg-base">
        {title}
      </Heading>
      <Button>Click me</Button>
    </div>
  );
}

export default MyComponent;
```

### Good Class Usage

```tsx
// ✅ Correct - using ui- prefixed classes
<div className="bg-ui-bg-base text-ui-fg-base border-ui-border-base">
  Content
</div>

// ❌ Avoid - custom colors not from preset
<div className="bg-blue-500 text-gray-800">
  Content
</div>
```
